  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of archived Alaska Medicaid Lybalvi (olanzapine/samidorphan) criteria, effective 2022-01-04. Both closed indications share all approval and denial gates. Failure to meet approval criteria is a denial.",
    "Bipolar I disorder includes acute treatment of manic or mixed episodes as monotherapy or adjunct to lithium or valproate, and maintenance monotherapy.",
    "Clinical facts, baseline documentation, ongoing monitoring and failure of at least two different atypical antipsychotics for at least 4 weeks each are attestations; evidence verification requires manual review.",
    "Denial criterion 5 is encoded as any strong CYP3A4 inducer, levodopa, or dopamine agonist use.",
    "Cautions (notes only): see package insert https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2021/213378s000lbl.pdf.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 1 year if disease improvement and stabilization are shown and there have been no adverse effects (including severe metabolic changes or tardive dyskinesia).",
    "Quantity (notes only): 30 tablets (1 tablet per day). max_units is null. Duration, reauthorization, cautions and quantity enforcement require manual review. PDL status unknown; no linked alternatives."
  ],
